<title>GERMANY: Waigel says to stick to 1997 budget.</title>
<headline>Waigel says to stick to 1997 budget.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>German Finance Minister Theo Waigel said he was determined to stick to his 1997 budget plans in spite of problems in the labour market.</p>
<p>&quot;We will stick to the key figures of the 1997 budget despite the risks from the labour market,&quot; Waigel told parliament.</p>
<p>Waigel plans to reduce federal outlays to 440 billion marks next year from a planned 451 billion this year. He aims for a federal deficit of 56.5 billion marks.</p>
<p>--Bonn newsroom, 49 228 26097150</p>
</text>
